# ============================================================================
# US SECURITIES - NOT NEEDED IN CONFIG
# ============================================================================
# US securities (VOO, VGK, GLD, IAU, etc.) are auto-detected correctly:
# - yfinance works with symbol as-is (no exchange suffix needed)
# - Currency defaults to USD
# - IBKR auto-population will handle these
#
# NO NEED TO LIST THEM HERE!

# ============================================================================
# CRYPTO - RARELY NEEDED IN CONFIG
# ============================================================================
# Crypto symbols are auto-detected and use USD by default.
# CoinMarketCap is primary source, yfinance is fallback.
#
# Only add entries here if you need to:
# - Force a specific provider (e.g., yfinance instead of CoinMarketCap)
# - Use non-USD currency (e.g., BTC in EUR)
#
# Example overrides (uncomment if needed):
#
# BTC:
#   yfinance_symbol: "BTC-USD"
#   currency: "USD"
#   provider: "yfinance"  # Force yfinance instead of CoinMarketCap
#
# ETH:
#   yfinance_symbol: "ETH-EUR"
#   currency: "EUR"
#   provider: "yfinance"  # Fetch ETH in EUR instead of USD

# ============================================================================
# SPECIAL CASES
# ============================================================================

# Physical gold (uses gold scraper, not market data sync)
# Listed here for documentation and to prevent accidental price sync
GOLDTHB:
  provider: "goldtraders_scraper"
  currency: "THB"
  description: "Physical Gold Baht (Gold Traders Thailand)"
  auto_sync: false # ← Important: Prevents inclusion in daily price sync

# ============================================================================
# STABLECOINS - GERMAN TAX COMPLIANCE
# ============================================================================
# Stablecoins (USDT, USDC, BUSD, DAI, TUSD, USDP) are CRYPTO ASSETS, not fiat.
#
# Portfolio Allocation:
#   - Stored in Portfolio 8 (Broker Cash Pool) for liquidity tracking
#   - But tracked as crypto for tax purposes (NOT cash)
#
# Tax Treatment (German Tax Law):
#   - Each stablecoin transaction is a TAXABLE EVENT
#   - Cost basis tracking required (acquisition price)
#   - FIFO allocation for lot tracking
#   - 1-year HODL rule applies (determines tax rate)
#
# Trading Behavior:
#   Example: Buy 0.01 BTC with 500 USDT creates TWO transactions:
#     1. type='exchange', symbol='USDT', qty=-500 (disposal, taxable) → Portfolio 8
#     2. type='exchange', symbol='BTC', qty=0.01 (acquisition) → Portfolio 6
#
# Price Tracking:
#   - Auto-synced by sync_crypto_prices() just like other crypto
#   - No symbol_mapping.yaml entries needed (default behavior)
#   - CoinMarketCap → yfinance fallback chain
#
# Implementation:
#   - Binance parsers detect stablecoin pairs automatically
#   - See: crud/parsers/binancecom_parser.py, binanceth_parser.py
#   - Stablecoin list: config/app_config.yaml (stablecoin_symbols)
